From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: H96 build <builder@h96-build>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/20] phy: rockchip: usbdp: keep U3 port off with 4 DP lanes,
 honour maximum-speed

When rockchip,dp-lane-mux assigns all four lanes to DP no lane is left
for USB3: do not enable UDPHY_MODE_USB for the u3-port. A
maximum-speed property on the u3-port child (legacy DTs) other than
super-speed selects high-speed only. Restores rkr5.1 and mainline
behaviour; fixes a dead USB port on usb@fc400000 with the board DTB.

Gated by DT content.

H96 series: ff042f9d1.
---
 drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c
index 135221238..7b8fa286b 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-usbdp.c
@@ -1670,7 +1670,15 @@ static int rockchip_udphy_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			phy_set_bus_width(phy, udphy->dp_lanes);
 			phy->attrs.max_link_rate = udphy_dp_get_max_link_rate(udphy, child_np);
 		} else if (of_node_name_eq(child_np, "u3-port")) {
-			udphy->mode |= UDPHY_MODE_USB;
+			const char *speed;
+
+			/* a 4-lane DP mux leaves no lane for USB3: keep the U3 port disabled */
+			if (udphy->dp_lanes < 4)
+				udphy->mode |= UDPHY_MODE_USB;
+			/* legacy DTs put maximum-speed on the u3-port child */
+			if (!of_property_read_string(child_np, "maximum-speed", &speed) &&
+			    !strstr(speed, "super-speed"))
+				udphy->hs = true;
 			phy = devm_phy_create(dev, child_np, &rockchip_u3phy_ops);
 			if (IS_ERR(phy)) {
 				dev_err(dev, "failed to create usb phy: %pOFn\n", child_np);
